// Script mode with a library import (libdemo layout): lib's signatures
// are inlined at compile time from the -I source directory, its code
// joins the link closure at load time from the prebuilt lib.ncu next to
// this unit. ctest has no exact-exit-code property, so the fixture
// self-checks the value and maps it to 0/9 (the same self-check +
// distinct-nonzero-exit shape libdemo_run uses; the exact
// top-level-return exit-code mapping is pinned by check_nlang_tool.py).
import lib;
if (lib.twice(21) == 42) { return 0; }
return 9;
